# Reverse proxy for bookmgr: terminates HTTPS (automatic Let's Encrypt
# certificate) and forwards plain HTTP to the FastAPI server running
# locally. Replace bookmgr.example.com with your actual domain; it must
# already resolve (DNS A/AAAA record) to this machine's public IP, and
# ports 80/443 must be reachable from the internet for the ACME challenge
# and HTTPS traffic.
#
# Run the FastAPI server with HOST=127.0.0.1 and COOKIE_SECURE=true so it
# only accepts connections from Caddy and marks the session cookie
# HTTPS-only (see README.md).
#
# Usage: caddy run --config deploy/Caddyfile

bookmgr.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
